--TEST--
Every `@tag` in a doc comment but `@see` and `@example` is `E0128`, and the one PHPDoc name whose answer is the signature gets its own help — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/doc-comments
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`: the set is closed, so
// every other `@tag` is a diagnostic. `@param` gets its own answer, since the
// signature already says it; an invented tag gets the rule itself.
/// Charges a card, in the smallest unit the currency has.
///
/// @param $cents the amount to charge
/// @ledger nothing reads this
final class Till {
    public static function charge(int $cents): int {
        return $cents;
    }
}
echo Till::charge(1), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0128]: `@param` is not a documentation tag
  --> %s:8:5
  |
8 | /// @param $cents the amount to charge
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not `@see` or `@example`
  = help: name the parameter in a sentence instead — its type is already in the signature

error[E0128]: `@ledger` is not a documentation tag
  --> %s:9:5
  |
9 | /// @ledger nothing reads this
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not `@see` or `@example`
  = help: a doc comment is Markdown plus `@see` and `@example`, and the set is closed (`rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`)

error: aborting due to 2 errors
